      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-03-14_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>C4ESHIRE CENTENARIAN.</head>
        <p>C4ESHIRE CENTENARIAN.</p>
        <p>Eaf„ , eqtkee-gllaY Mrs. Nannie Turner, the old utt • " the Marquis of Cholmondeley's tno,,nl.tined her hundred and first birthday. - post brought old Nannie many e4L'ehio„ll(l gifts, and there was one \ from the lqq)rat.;:less of Chohnondeley. The event was thliptie Ta with a family birthday party. Old dreli t' over forty grand and great grand- 441er • ' "RI one of her relatives is a labour loa Australia.</p>
