        <p>• When food lies undigested in the stomach it ferments and gas forms. This gas distends the stomach and presses on the heart, causing a pain that sometimes arouses fear of heart trouble. The condition in which gas forms is (guise(' by a lack of rich red blood resulting in deficient nerve force. It is a condition that calls (ova tonic. Dr. Williams' Pink Pills, a tonic for the blood nervk, have been: used with great success in the treatment of this form of stomach trouble. eohtbailis.in the morning followed by brisk friction with a rough towel will help in stimul;ifing the circulation, lint a tonic treat- ment with Dr. Williams' Pink Pills by build- ing up the blood, restoring the nerve force and making the, stomach able to do its:work gives the most lasting benefit. With the use of these Pills the appetite increases, ingestion becomes 'formal and iniprovetnent in the general ltealth 'follows with certainty. You are tryin,,,, Am experiment whew you take Dr, ,Williants' Pink Pills: They' cannot *harm the most delicate system. 'You can get Dr. Williams' Pink Pills at the licare4 dealers; or, if preferred, send direct to Dr. Williams' Medicine Co., 46,1101b0rn-viaduct, London, post free 2/9 a box. or 13/9 for six. copy of the diet book, " What to Eat and How to Eat," will be sent to you free by the Book Dept.,. 46, •Ifolboro-vhuluet.</p>
