        <p>......,... Single Daffodil.—l, Rose Saddler and Frank Worsley; 2, James Hardman, Bertie Smallwood and John Hill; •3, Albert Mather, Thonms Richardson and Eva Brookes; he, Dorothy Leigh; c, Millie Northorn and James Turner, Narcissus.-1, Cyril Pitchford. ' Drawings.—Age-14: 1, 11. Cross; 2, C. Craske and 11. Birks. Age 13: 1, W. Twiss and S. Spittle; 2, S. Hall and S. Eccleston; 3, L. Fleming and H. Barlow. Age 12: 1, E. Beddall and J. Millington; 2, J. Ball and H. Simcock ; 3, H. Wright, J. Parfitt and S. Taylor. Age 11: 1, E. Twiss; 2, S. Clare, R. Hall and W. Leices- ter; 3, C. Ashley and A. Connor. Age 10: 1, M. Bibby; 2, M. Hazledine and S. Leigh; 3, H. 23,, E. TNy ji iii•eurn, Bingham, 11. Stillingfleet and F. Pitchford. i Crayon Drawings.—Age 13: 1, S. Hall, N. gl:o:,aJr.lo:trOoWsli.. 1 Shaw; 3, E. Thornley, D. Eccleston, C. Makin, T. Fernehough. Age 12: 1,11. Lightfoot; 2, W. j Davies, H. Cross; Age 10: 1, J. 'Warburton ; 2. T. Bibby. Age 8 and 9: 1, T. Litherland; 2, SAigmeclolek:,l.," J. Ball;stitt o n . V. Millington ; 3. S. Woodward. . Paintings.—Age 14: 1, J. Ormesby: 2, C. Cra§lie; 3, M. Stewart Age 13: 1. W. Shaw, J• Armstrong; 2, J. Leigh; 3. F. Ifeesnm, C. Makin . . 'Age 12: 1, J. Ball, If. Wright: 2. L. Armitage, W. Simcock. Age 10: 1, F. Wilkinson.</p>
