      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-03-14_WidnesExaminer_art0066" n="art0066">
        <p>THE EXAMINER, SATURDAY, MARCH 14, 1914</p>
        <p>implicitly relied upon, and that his name cin a balance sheet always inspires confidence. (Ap- plause.) ,</p>
        <p>The resolution was carried unanimously.</p>
        <p>Mr. VOISEY : Gentlemen, I am obliged for your renewed confidence in me, and I take the oppor- tunity to congratulate the directors on this very excellent balance sheet. It is not my business at this Meeting to go into the balance sheet, but I quite endorse what has been said. The com- pany, in my opinion, is in a thoroughly sound and strong position. (Applause.)</p>
