      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-03-14_WidnesExaminer_art0088" n="art0088">
        <head>LICENSEE'S FRIENDS. Billiard Match and an Invitation.</head>
        <p>THE LICENSEE'S FRIENDS. Billiard Match and an Invitation.</p>
        <p>'AII4, case, which aroused great public 't,z7rest, was heard at the Borough Police 4.141,44 on Tuesday, when a number of men were . ki..."`trioned for having been on the licensed pre. ' 4478 Of the Golden Lion Hotel, Knutsford-road, ke-',llB I prohibited hours on February 19th. The the- 81-bumoned before Councillor H. Roberts (in •)ikil'air), Mr. C. Jackson Holmes and Mr. T. Ilt 1•, were • William Fell, 4, Cumberland- ,' b./4Z; Isaac 'Newell, 34, Barry-street; Alfred 4, Clifton-street; Walter Whittle, 209, °l•d-road; Thomas Clarke, 10, Clifton. • `trtt ' Willi and George Newell, 10, Miller- el t. , am l,,llornas Farmer, 71, New-road; John ~1 0-'141: `.;ritchley 18, Hughes-street; and Joseph ti.tti,llhol6.' ,40,t, Knu'tsford-road.—.Mr. Gilbert Jor- T-NbPster (instructed by Mr. T. S. Steel) ••• rOtr - - - - •</p>
        <p>r the defendants. E't Constable opened the case.</p>
        <p>hIIe'INGING AND SHOUTING. .11,?,_1',.84111'4,wkins said at 11.15 p.m. he was in 1,•,o St street, and saw all the defendants, eY 'h exception of Critchley and Loker 4„114 sl.ne,..r:e under the influence of Jrinit, sjllglng and obstructing the footo.atn -1 m ' thie e and they became quiet _or a Cutler t(1 17 (lig-II:It When, a in Bridge-street they resumed wed 4,l4hance. Witness and P.C. ppe.La along here Knutsford-road, they _ f",en "xlayes' who said he had cautioned the their behaviour. They lost sight of Carklants, but, on nearing the Golden Lion Wa.,, 4_ll a door close. In consequence of what '" went to the hotel and saw ness JUDIE'S Kay. On askel if he t,stlendß in, en on his premises Kay replied, "yes, ,°1 rnin" Witness said he -would like Joees:f.- a word with them, and Kay gave him thMer tile Premises. On entering a zoom the 'I 8 .°llrld•th •I t n round a • Ivitl • • e elg • • t f them tltth/ Dint glasses of beer in front o . 144•11,,t5. ritteln,:lrla Locker were also there. Defend- 'te toi and addresses were taken, and they a they would be reported. On returning</p>
        <p>SYM IN GT igi Trade COF ff,NCE</p>
        <p>P in The Coffee Maid, of Symington's, my:: e morning, sleepy and cold, presto, change I—and you're WharscillicerY and bold, c snagie? How is it done? just try a cup ofSYMINGTON." :nos. sranNoms s, fittlefirth sad Undo.</p>
