      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-03-14_WidnesExaminer_art0199" n="art0199">
        <head>FINAL VISIT</head>
        <p>FINAL VISIT</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>On Wednesday nest I must definitely close my visits to Warrington, as I am booked to visit other districts immediately afterwards. This will be my last visit here for four years; not until 1918 will I be able to visit you 'again so that those who have been putting off for so long must consult me now, or r otherwise their chance of happiness and relief will be gone. If you do not wish to adopt my advice there is no charge; you are under no obligoattion whatever. My appliances have been supplied to the London Hospital and every other large medical institution in the country, and thny are strongly recommended by the medical profession; in fact, I number several doctors' wives amongst my patients—sure proof of the efficacy of my Belts.</p>
        <p>Note Date of Final Visit. CONSULT ME ON WEDNESDAY NEXT. Ruptures, Women's Internal Weaknesses, Displacement, etc., Cured and Relic%fed Without Operations or Internal Implements.</p>
        <p>Our delicate organisations render us liable to contract internal ailments which, if not attended to in time, may cause us years of suffering. Most women, especially the younger ones, generally do their utmost to keep the nature of their ailments to themselves, in many cases not even telling their own relatives—this no doubt from a sense of false modesty. Any thought of consulting a specialist is immedi- ately stampeded. Why do you not ac- cept the inevitable and consult a lady specialist—one of your own sex, who has had over twenty years' experience amongst cases similar to yours, and who has cured and relieved over 90,000! Whether it be internal weak- ness, displacement, rupture, or kindred complaints, I can cure you. Read these Local Testimonials.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON LETTER.</p>
        <p>LYMM TESTIMONIAL.</p>
        <p>"Dear Madam,—You will be pleased to learn that already I have derived much benefit from your Rupture Belt. Although I have only worn it a fort- night I feel like a new woman. If I make the same progress (and I am sure I will) I will be strong and well again in a very few weeks."—Mrs. J. PRESTON BROOK EVIDENCE. " Dear Madam,—lt is with feelings of the utmost gratitude that I pen the following to tell you of the relief I have already had from wearing the appliance. It seems wonderful that such a change could have been effected in two weeks only. I feel nearly as strong as ever I was."—Mrs. E. G. A WIDNES LADY writes! "Dear Madam,—l can honestly say that your claim to cure internal weak- ness without operations has been well sustained in my case. I have tried several so-called cures with unsatis- factory results. However, your treat- ment, which causes no inconvenience, has already done me a great amount of good."</p>
        <p>"Dear . Madam, Your crusade against m i the use of internal instru- ents s, I should imagine, one of the greatest blessings bestowed on us poor women who have been deluded into the use of same. On second thoughts, it appears obvious that such methods cannot do the patient any good; at least this was my. experience. How- ever, after adopting your treatment for a fortnight only, I am already greatly improved, and well on the way to my former good health."</p>
        <p>FURTHER WARRINGTON PROOF.</p>
        <p>A lady to whom I had supplied a belt a fortnight previous came to see me to express her thanks for the way my appliance had cured her. She said that previous to wearing it she had not been able to do any work dur- ing the past five years, and yet, after wearing the belt only a fortnight, she could get about as well as ever. In fact, she walked about four miles to see me.</p>
        <p>ALL. ADVICE FREE. MRS. CIAILIZA E. SLATER Visits WARRINGTON on WEDNESDAY NEXT (March 18th). DRUIDS' HALL. Hours. 2 to 5. Write for New Illustrated Booklet, "Why Internal Instruments slould not be worn,'' to Mrs. CLARA E. SLATER, Belgrano, Finsbury Park, London, N.</p>
