        <p>Work, whether bodilY mental, uses -up the tissues of the budy. The,4e mast be replaced by food. Discerning folk find out IT experience the class of diet which gives them a feeling of re_ or newed strength, vigour and vitality. There is (MO SUbStallee---11kOVIdC41 IT Nature—whieli adds to, or rather proriqcs, the food value of any dish whenever it appeifr4, and hat tis gratie sugar. From time immm ugar eorial, grai)e s h as bene- fited niankind, for it is a food of great potener, ,-et easily digested. (rape augur is found in abundance in the Greek ‘--"rralit, the little fruit that hae been aptly• described as " full of flour- of Numerous exapuileg could be quoted of the wonderful effects of a liberal diet of cur- rants. Weaklings have- been strengthened by them, people whose apretites were hopelesslY flagging have beeii tem! ted to eat, and thereby regained health by using plenty of Currants. Try them this way-to-day.</p>
