      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-03-14_WidnesExaminer_art0221" n="art0221">
        <head>New Music.</head>
        <p>New Music.</p>
        <p>Messrs. Ascheberg, Hopwood and Crew, Ltd, The Garden of England. A Kentish Song-Cycle. Written by Francis Barron and inusie by Herbert Goldstein. 3s. net.</p>
        <p>This little album contains four very pretty songs about the county of Kent. They are suit- able for concert work, and very effective in every way. The\ song " The Cherry Pickers " is sure to become a favourite, and the musie in key E is very catchy and tuneful. • The little book as a ballad album ought to have a- ready sale and become popular. The music is very attractive. Martita Tango Argentine. By Julio Pizzarro. Prfce is. lid. net.</p>
        <p>- After a short introduction the chief theme appears in key B- flat, then it goes tunefully into key E flat, where the movement is delight- ful and very taking; the piece then finishes in the original key. It is sure to be appreciated by dancers.. It is not suitable for beginners, but would be useful for more advanced stu- dents.</p>
        <p>The death is announced near Maeroom, County Cork, of Daniel Mullane, who is stated to have reached the age of DO years. lie was an agricultural labourer and continued active up to .a few months ago.</p>
